<!--
   QML card back style "Disco".

   A mirror ball under black light - the counterpart to the table style "disco"
   and to the card deck "blacklight_4c". The ball is a real facetted sphere:
   a latitude/longitude grid, orthographically projected, the back face
   discarded, every facet diffusely lit with a hard specular highlight; nearly
   half of the mirrors catch the black light colours of the deck (magenta, cyan,
   amber, violet). The specks of light on the card stock are what the ball
   throws into the room.

   Everything is built from paths and gradients - QtSvg does not know filters.
